<%# THE STRIP (Shop manual spec §7 and §11.2; design-system.md rules 7 to 9). It replaced the rail and
    the top bar: the wordmark (Home), the four places, Search, one Add, and the account button.

    THE FOUR PLACES ARE ALWAYS ALL FOUR, and at most one is lit — `ShellHelper#sidebar_current`
    decides, and the place is derived from its key (`sidebar_place`), so the strip, the column and the
    phone tab bar cannot disagree. Home, Search, Settings and Help light none.

    Locals: column (whether the page has a left column, so the Contents button that opens it as a
    sheet below 960px has something to open). %>
<header class="strip">
  <% if column %>
    <%# BELOW 960PX THE COLUMN IS A SHEET, and this opens it (shell_controller.js): focus moves into
        the sheet, and Escape, the scrim or this button again closes it and hands focus back here. %>
    <button type="button" class="strip-contents" aria-label="Contents" title="Contents" aria-controls="column" aria-expanded="false"
            data-shell-target="contents" data-action="shell#toggleColumn">
      <%= rail_icon(:contents) %><span class="strip-contents-label">Contents</span>
    </button>
  <% end %>
  <%= link_to root_path, class: "brand strip-brand", "aria-label": "Tinkerex home" do %>
    <span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="brand-name">Tinkerex</span>
  <% end %>

  <nav class="strip-places" aria-label="Main">
    <% strip_places.each do |place, label, path, _icon| %>
      <%= link_to label, path, class: "strip-place", "aria-current": place_aria(place) %>
    <% end %>
  </nav>

  <%# THE RIGHT-HAND GROUP, pushed to the strip's right edge: Search, Add, the account button. %>
  <div class="strip-end">
  <%= form_with url: search_path, method: :get, class: "strip-search", role: "search",
                data: { turbo: false } do %>
    <%= rail_icon(:search) %>
    <%# ALWAYS BLANK, DELIBERATELY -- @q IS ALSO THE NAME FilesController, InventoryItemsController
        AND SearchController ITSELF GIVE THEIR OWN IVARS, and echoing whichever one the current
        request happens to carry would leak one page's private local filter (Files', Inventory's)
        into a box that means something else (search EVERYTHING). SearchController's OWN page has its
        own big search-toolbar input for that job (search/index.html.erb) -- this is the entry point,
        not a second display of the last query. shell_controller.js finds this field through its
        `search` target for `/` and Ctrl/Cmd-K (spec §11.5); the hint shows `/`, and the title names
        the chord for this platform (ShellHelper#search_shortcut, UX audit A7). %>
    <input type="search" name="q" placeholder="Search everything" aria-label="Search everything"
           title="Search everything (/ or <%= search_shortcut %>)"
           aria-keyshortcuts="<%= ShellHelper::SEARCH_KEYS %>" autocomplete="off" data-shell-target="search">
    <kbd class="strip-kbd" aria-hidden="true">/</kbd>
  <% end %>
  <%# BELOW 720PX THE BOX IS THIS ICON, a link to the Search page, whose own box takes the query. %>
  <%= link_to search_path, class: "strip-search-link", "aria-label": "Search", title: "Search" do %>
    <%= rail_icon(:search) %>
  <% end %>

  <%= render "layouts/strip_add" %>

  <%# THE ACCOUNT BUTTON'S MENU holds what the rail's foot and the phone's More sheet held: Settings,
      Account and Help (each keeps its page), the theme choice, and Sign out. A `details.menu`, so it
      opens with no JavaScript; menu_controller.js closes it on an outside click and on Escape,
      returning focus to the button. None of its links is lit: Settings and Help light no place
      (spec §11.2), and on their pages the column lights the row. %>
  <details class="menu strip-account" data-controller="menu">
    <summary class="strip-account-btn" aria-label="Account: settings, theme, help, sign out"
             title="<%= current_user.email %>"><%= account_initial %></summary>
    <div class="menu-list strip-account-menu">
      <p class="strip-account-email" title="<%= current_user.email %>"><%= current_user.email %></p>
      <div class="menu-sep" role="separator"></div>
      <%= link_to settings_path, class: "menu-item" do %><%= rail_icon(:settings) %><span>Settings</span><% end %>
      <%= link_to edit_user_registration_path, class: "menu-item" do %><%= rail_icon(:account) %><span>Account</span><% end %>
      <%= link_to help_path, class: "menu-item" do %><%= rail_icon(:help) %><span>Help</span><% end %>
      <div class="menu-sep" role="separator"></div>
      <%# The Settings page's own three-way choice (settings/_theme), so the two cannot disagree; every
          instance follows a change made in another at once (theme_controller.js broadcasts it). %>
      <div class="strip-account-theme">
        <span class="strip-account-label">Theme</span>
        <%= render "settings/theme" %>
      </div>
      <div class="menu-sep" role="separator"></div>
      <%= button_to destroy_user_session_path, method: :delete, class: "menu-item" do %>
        <%= rail_icon(:sign_out) %><span>Sign out</span>
      <% end %>
    </div>
  </details>
  </div>
</header>
